Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0117, Phase 11 iter K Cand #1 -- drawTileFast inline).
Bypass Renderer::drawSurface entry chain for FG-tilemap drawcalls.
Wave-25 (slot 0111) measured dispatch_overhead_per_tile_us = 32.4 us
x 329 visible tiles ~ 10.7 ms / flip of pure overhead BEFORE the
inner `_blit_indexed` body fires -- RAII `_DrawcallTimer` 2x ns reads,
NULL check, 6x `*scale` (=1) multiplies, `_need_clip` branch,
`_bump_alpha_count` function call, `_try_fast_blit` 12-arg call with
5-condition validation, `_bump_drawcall` 2 increments,
`_record_dirty_rect` bbox accumulator. Tilemap call sites GUARANTEE
all the validation passes (tilesheet.alpha=255 always, INDEX8<->INDEX8
post-Wave-16, 320x240 window locked at boot, scale=1, no clip). So
the entire validation chain is wasted work on the dominant ~150
calls / flip path.

Mechanism (3 new entry points + 1 call-site change + 1 killswitch):

  Renderer::drawTileFast(Surface*, x, y, srcx, srcy)
    -- drains _renderer_queue_dirty (correctness; preserves z-order
      with prior slow-path commands)
    -- pre-computes 16x16 srcrect/dstrect inline (TILE_W/TILE_H from
      Tileset.h)
    -- calls _blit_indexed directly with src->surfaceCpu(),
      src->colorkey(), src->hasColorkey()
    -- skips _DrawcallTimer / _bump_alpha_count / _bump_drawcall /
      _record_dirty_rect / _try_fast_blit's validation gate

  Tileset::drawTileFast(x, y, t)
    -- same src-rect math as drawTile (tile-index -> 16-tiles-per-row
      sheet coordinates)
    -- adds NULL-tileset guard (drawSurface's NULL check is dropped
      by drawTileFast; this single Tileset-level guard preserves
      semantics cheaply -- branch predicted-not-taken in steady state)
    -- delegates to Renderer::drawTileFast

  map.cpp _tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop:
    -- reads `drawtile_fast_on` (cached static-const-bool from
      env_var_helper) once per call entry -- -O2 hoists the per-
      tile loop guard
    -- dominant else-branch path (the ~150 tiles/flip drawTile case):
      `if (drawtile_fast_on) tileset.drawTileFast(...) else
       tileset.drawTile(...)` -- preserves wave-25 RDTSC bracket
      around the call (g_mds_tfg_drawtile_total_ns + count) so
      iter-K-1 can A/B drawtile_per_us between killswitch=ON vs
      killswitch=OFF

  Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DRAWTILE_FAST=0 strict-match (only
  literal "0" disables; mirror of patch 0088 / 0093 / 0115's
  inverse-killswitch convention). Default ON. Lambda in
  _abl_drawtile_fast() per the patch-0088 pattern. Per
  env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md: documented in docs/BOOT.md
  alongside slot 0113 / 0115.

Wave-25 instrumentation interaction (CRITICAL):
  _blit_indexed bracket gates on g_mds_tfg_loop_active flag, set by
  map.cpp's FG-loop entry/exit when foreground == TA_FOREGROUND AND
  MDS_TFG_INSTR=1. drawTileFast still calls _blit_indexed -> the
  blit_indexed_per_us / count counters continue to fire correctly.
  drawtile_per_us / count counters at the map.cpp call site also
  still fire (they're outside drawTileFast, wrapping the call). So
  the contract:
    drawtile_per_us -> expected to DROP from ~58.0 us (iter J) toward
                      blit_indexed_per_us (~25.7 us iter J) when
                      killswitch=ON
    dispatch_overhead_per_tile_us = drawtile_per_us -
                      blit_indexed_per_us -> expected to DROP from
                      ~32.4 us toward 0 when killswitch=ON
  iter-K-1 PLAY1 (drawTileFast=ON) vs PLAY2 (drawTileFast=OFF)
  delta isolates the lever. Per dosbox_not_perf_proxy.md +
  dosbox_scales_per_code_path.md: real-HW PODP-OD-83 is the load-
  bearing gate; DOSBox-X scaling is 0.81x-286x per code path.

Predicted savings (per perf_predictions_unreliable.md honesty
discipline; predictions historically wrong 5-30x):
  Range -3 to -5 ms / flip per FPS-DEEPDIVE sec. 2 row #1.
  Iter K-1 real-HW measurement -> confirm or pressure-test.
  Outside that range = investigate per
  measurements_above_prediction_are_red_flags.md.

Trade-offs called out (per pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md):
  - _bump_drawcall is skipped: tilemap drawcalls don't bump engine-
    wide drawcall counters under killswitch=ON. The aggregate
    `_drawcalls_total` field in [drawcall tally] log lines under-
    counts by ~150/flip. Counter is informational, not essential.
  - _record_dirty_rect is skipped: tilemap drawcalls don't update
    `_dirty_rects` bbox accumulator. Default-config full-refresh
    fires every flip per slot 0085 (PREVFRAME_DIFF default OFF since
    wave-17.6); partial-flush via prev-frame-diff path uses per-
    scanline memcmp -- independent of `_dirty_rects`. So default
    config: no behavior change. Opt-in PREVFRAME_DIFF + drawTile-
    Fast combo: tilemap regions become "dirty everywhere full-flush"
    by virtue of memcmp-against-prev-frame finding them changed.
    Acceptable.
  - _bump_alpha_count is skipped: tilesheet alpha is always 255 so
    the `nonopaque / total` ratio in the alpha audit log is
    unaffected. Total drawcall count under-counts by ~150/flip but
    the `_alpha_nonopaque_drawcalls / _alpha_total_drawcalls`
    fraction is unchanged.
  - drawSurface NULL-texture diagnostic skipped: the Tileset-level
    NULL guard (`if (!_tileset) return;` at the top of drawTileFast)
    catches the only realistic failure mode (missing tilesheet
    file). drawSurface's full _log_null_tex pump for arbitrary
    Surface NULLs is overkill for this path.

Build (DOSBox-X smoke pre-iter-K-1):
  build SHA: 9719eb74af5bc791105ef5c9bb86640d45bb7677b6a7a15063c11b9c0b0df48f
  strings markers verified embedded:
    - "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DRAWTILE_FAST" (env-var symbol)
    - "_ZN3NXE8Graphics8Renderer12drawTileFastE..." (mangled symbol)
    - "_ZN3NXE8Graphics7Tileset12drawTileFastE..." (mangled symbol)

Out of scope (per silent_narrow_pattern.md):
  - drawSurface fast-fast-path for non-tilemap paths (sprites, HUD).
    Sprites need _bump_drawcall + dirty-rect + alpha audit because
    those paths exercise alpha<255 + mirror + clip variability.
    drawTileFast's invariant assumptions don't hold for sprites.
  - Cached srcrect tuple optimization (the per-call srcx/srcy ->
    16x16 stamp recomputes 2 multiplies + 2 modulos per call).
    Optimizing that would save ~5-10 cycles per tile = 1-2 us / flip
    -- below noise floor. Defer until iter L if other levers exhaust.

